## Example script

```python
from mythtv_api import MythTVClient


def main():
    myth = MythTVClient("localhost")

    print("Host:")
    print(myth.myth.get_host_name())

    print()
    print("Backend info:")
    print(myth.myth.get_backend_info())

    print()
    print("Recordings:")
    recordings = myth.dvr.get_recorded_list(count=10)

    programs = (
        recordings
        .get("ProgramList", {})
        .get("Programs", [])
    )

    for program in programs:
        title = program.get("Title")
        subtitle = program.get("SubTitle")
        chan_id = program.get("Channel", {}).get("ChanId")
        start_time = program.get("StartTime")

        print(f"- {title} - {subtitle} [{chan_id}, {start_time}]")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
```

---

## Notes

Most MythTV service endpoints are available under URLs like:

```text
http://BACKEND:6544/Myth/GetHostName
http://BACKEND:6544/Dvr/GetRecordedList
http://BACKEND:6544/Guide/GetProgramGuide
http://BACKEND:6544/Channel/GetChannelInfoList
http://BACKEND:6544/Content/GetRecording
```

This library automatically appends:

```text
format=json
```

to non-binary API requests.

For binary endpoints such as recordings, preview images, channel icons, and files, use `get_raw()` or the helper methods under `myth.content`.

