# mythtv-api

A small Python client for the MythTV Services API.

MythTV usually exposes its backend HTTP Services API on port `6544`.

## Installation

For local development:

```bash
pip install -e .
```

## Basic usage

```python
from mythtv_api import MythTVClient

myth = MythTVClient("192.168.1.50")

print(myth.myth.get_host_name())

recordings = myth.dvr.get_recorded_list()
print(recordings)
```

## With authentication

```python
from mythtv_api import MythTVClient

myth = MythTVClient(
    "192.168.1.50",
    username="mythtv",
    password="password",
)

print(myth.myth.get_backend_info())
```

## Get upcoming recordings

```python
from mythtv_api import MythTVClient

myth = MythTVClient("mythbackend.local")

upcoming = myth.dvr.get_upcoming_list(count=20)

for item in upcoming["ProgramList"]["Programs"]:
    print(item["Title"], item["StartTime"])
```

## Get recorded programs

```python
from mythtv_api import MythTVClient

myth = MythTVClient("mythbackend.local")

recordings = myth.dvr.get_recorded_list()

for program in recordings["ProgramList"]["Programs"]:
    print(program["Title"], program["SubTitle"])
```

